            <ArticleTitle>Permanent anterior dislocation of the proximal tibiofibular joint.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>240-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two patients with permanent dislocation of the proximal tibiofibular joint and no history of trauma. Both needed operation, one for persistent pain and the other for common peroneal nerve involvement, and both had a good result.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
